########## KNOWN DEVIATION from acceptance #2 (literal command form) ##########
# Acceptance #2 literally specifies:
#   podman run --rm localhost/alma:d7-hermes hermes --version
# This returns RC=255 with no stdout because the base image — like every bootc
# image in this repo — sets ENTRYPOINT [ "/sbin/init" ] (Containerfile line 194).
# Podman therefore runs "/sbin/init hermes --version", i.e. systemd treats
# "hermes --version" as *unit arguments*, not as a command to exec.
#
# The CLI itself is correct and reachable — see [2b], [2d] and [4] — it just
# needs the image entrypoint cleared, exactly as this repo already does for
# bootc images (cf. commit c817a7a1, "Clear entrypoint ... because bootc images
# ship ENTRYPOINT [/sbin/init]"):
#   podman run --rm --entrypoint '' localhost/alma:d7-hermes hermes --version   -> works
#   just hermes alma d7-hermes --version                                        -> works (recipe clears it)
#
# The spec's own design-decision #5 recipe example has the same interaction;
# the shipped recipe adds --entrypoint "" to handle it. Changing the shared
# base image's ENTRYPOINT was rejected as out of scope: every derived image
# (hci/k3s/dx/webtop/...) builds FROM this base and relies on it for systemd boot.
